    correct: 1,
    explain: "<b>Verify explicitly</b> means evaluating <em>every</em> request against the signals of the moment, not trusting an authentication from hours ago. It is fixed with sign-in frequency, <b>CAE</b> and, for critical operations, recent strong authentication. Assume breach and least privilege are the other two principles and describe different problems. And the fourth option names the right principle with a measure that has nothing to do with it. <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-continuous-access-evaluation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microsoft Learn ↗</a>",
