    explain: "<b>Report-only mode</b> evaluates the policy on every real sign-in and records the outcome <em>without applying it</em>: that is precisely \"knowing who it would block without blocking\". <b>What If</b> checks specific cases before you even publish it. The pilot already blocks a hundred people. Apply-and-roll-back blocks everyone. And rebuilding it by hand in KQL approximates with queries what the platform computes exactly. <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-report-only\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microsoft Learn ↗</a>",
